Subject: [PATCH] [mlir] The region inliner stops at an early exit

On top of llvm/llvm-project#166688. `InlineRegionBranchOp` inlines an op
when `computeSingleAcyclicRegionBranchPath` finds one path through it
from "parent" back to its results. Once an exit crosses the op, a region
ending in that exit has, as its one successor, a region or the results of
the exit's target, an enclosing op. The path follows it into the target,
which the pattern does not own: the pattern then inlines the region,
erases the exit and asks the op for the target's inputs, which asserts in
a build with assertions, and returns "path ends after a different
operation" after it has changed the IR. `scf.if %true { scf.break ... }`
reaches it through `scf.if`'s registration of the pattern.

The path now ends, unmatched, at a successor the op does not own
(`getRegionBranchSuccessorOwner`), before anything is changed.
---
diff --git a/mlir/lib/Interfaces/ControlFlowInterfaces.cpp b/mlir/lib/Interfaces/ControlFlowInterfaces.cpp
index 06deedb5..c53fd9bc 100644
--- a/mlir/lib/Interfaces/ControlFlowInterfaces.cpp
+++ b/mlir/lib/Interfaces/ControlFlowInterfaces.cpp
@@ -1252,6 +1252,11 @@ computeSingleAcyclicRegionBranchPath(RegionBranchOpInterface op) {
       // through the region branch op.
       return {};
     }
+    if (getRegionBranchSuccessorOwner(successors.front()) != op) {
+      // The path leaves the op through an early exit to a region or the
+      // results of an enclosing op, which this op does not own.
+      return {};
+    }
     path.push_back(successors.front());
     if (successors.front().isOperation()) {
       // Found path that ends after an operation.
